#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073481 :question/id #uuid "b1d34db3-7f30-5a8c-b233-fd955ac656f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14011" :question/problem "At how many points do the lines $x - 2y = 2$ and $10y - 5x = -10$ intersect?" :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n{x - 2y = 2; 10y - 5x =-10\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx - 2y &= 2 \\\\\nx &= 2y + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=2y+2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10y - 5x &= -10 \\\\\n10y - 5(2y + 2) &= -10 \\\\\n10y - 10y - 10 &= -10 \\\\\n- 10 &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049869 :topic/math-academy-id 408 :topic/title "Calculating the Intersection of Two Lines"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050245 :topic/math-academy-id 837 :topic/title "Parallel Lines in the Coordinate Plane"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561267 :question-generator/id #uuid "fc2c9fcc-ff7e-5428-8e69-97128784c006" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186073777.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4213192-05bd-5441-ab8f-5601edb4f46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070315} {:answer/id #uuid "d06783b6-d3ed-5f45-826b-a57ede5f7c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070316} {:answer/id #uuid "3a739d2b-bb1e-5a44-b0f7-82240d439868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070317}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2054f218-d7fb-5f4b-bb1e-7462237fd4e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070314}] :question/id #uuid "dffc4e2c-f9ea-5274-92e6-4d3948a4c014" :question/math-academy-id "q-211986" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 2x - y =-2, l_{2}: 6x - 3y =-12$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b83e75eb-68ab-567d-a460-9470152445c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070381} {:answer/id #uuid "fb057ae1-6d19-5e10-9555-8ef14e34ac05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070382} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6737ed-0efb-5044-904e-0bbf76ec3016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070383}] :answer-field/id #uuid "19065220-42bb-5118-b439-9be235fa2f10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070380}] :question/id #uuid "c2c1547a-6290-54a8-97be-3db72633dabf" :question/math-academy-id "q-237095" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = 3x - 4, l_{2}: 12x - 4y = 16$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561203 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "866eae0c-01b3-50bf-b526-86a0c6cac6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561230} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa7f187-7fdf-5a83-ab02-69b55dfb828f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561244} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c3ac96-f810-55fd-8221-e27eafaa255a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "866eae0c-01b3-50bf-b526-86a0c6cac6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561230} :answer-field/id #uuid "8500c6f6-dcab-5691-9d28-5480f89255f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561229}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a462c5e-dc46-5cbd-908d-8873a5836bec" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = x + 6, l_{2}: -3x + 3y = 18$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x + 6 \\\\ -3x + 3y &= 18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x + 6\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x + 6\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 3y &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3\\left(x + 6\\right) &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3x + 18 &= 18 \\\\\n18 &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75689f6e-65af-5364-b427-d0d53ea942af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561221} {:answer/id #uuid "79766299-4422-5446-8123-6c952ce516d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561225} {:answer/id #uuid "9eff61d3-41d1-56c6-bd82-959956a2ca75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79766299-4422-5446-8123-6c952ce516d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561225} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec6e71b-2b03-5a5a-9cc6-7eb21d9e2203" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561198}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c389456-1e7f-570a-b81d-ee3996221d09" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 5x - 2y =-1, l_{2}: -5x + 2y = 1$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 2y &=-1 \\\\ -5x + 2y &= 1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 2y &=-1 \\\\\n-2y &= -5x - 1 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-5x - 1}{-2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + 2y &= 1 \\\\\n-5x + 2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) &= 1 \\\\\n-5x + 5x + 1 &= 1 \\\\\n1 &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9164734a-796f-5af8-ac94-62a22713d23c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561234} {:answer/id #uuid "c60ae584-a9c5-5da2-b67b-9cea1d5ceb12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561246} {:answer/id #uuid "f5850239-8333-5a95-b556-84d53e0aa3e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9164734a-796f-5af8-ac94-62a22713d23c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561234} :answer-field/id #uuid "8afb3dd7-ffd1-50e9-b1b9-598ad7c3ec84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5dcff32d-252d-58bc-9fa9-cb87cd485a01" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 2x - 3y = 0, l_{2}: 6x - 9y = 0$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - 3y &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 9y &= 0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - 3y &= 0 \\\\\n-3y &= -2x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-2x}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}x\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - 9y &= 0 \\\\\n6x - 9\\left(\\frac{2}{3}x\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n6x - 6x &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13da69cb-99ca-554d-8d6d-4260e2aaf8e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561195} {:answer/id #uuid "4417ae70-0890-5813-a5ad-6509930c237e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561206} {:answer/id #uuid "73ba1cde-65b2-5df1-8173-f771c3abe4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73ba1cde-65b2-5df1-8173-f771c3abe4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561220} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b90caf-daee-5b7f-adfd-50fdc0c131c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6542765a-dbf6-5f4b-aedd-6339210b9996" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -5x + y =-1, l_{2}: 10x - 2y = 2$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x + y &=-1 \\\\ 10x - 2y &= 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= 5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x - 2y &= 2 \\\\\n10x - 2\\left(5x - 1\\right) &= 2 \\\\\n10x - 10x + 2 &= 2 \\\\\n2 &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28deb832-44b2-579c-bb80-e65dc4c0107e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561199} {:answer/id #uuid "6f64462a-0a21-5bfe-90c2-09bf574953ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561219} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f350c-25be-5a95-b053-4cbb5ed6e773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f350c-25be-5a95-b053-4cbb5ed6e773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561258} :answer-field/id #uuid "087a9931-aed8-58f6-9406-32b8d1499065" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76b29f4c-d2f7-5be9-99e6-f351f6d667d5" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = -5x - 5, l_{2}: 25x + 5y =-20$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= -5x - 5 \\\\ 25x + 5y &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = -5x - 5\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25x + 5y &=-20 \\\\\n25x + 5\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -20 \\\\\n25x - 25x - 25 &= -20 \\\\\n-25 &= -20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9537567-1850-5466-995f-5f2a3e4745df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561243} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40c9bc-94bd-5b2a-ac25-2906284d6dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561251} {:answer/id #uuid "cdeed473-c033-56b5-80e0-c80a74ce7f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdeed473-c033-56b5-80e0-c80a74ce7f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561252} :answer-field/id #uuid "47b67ab5-2541-51b1-b6af-87cd3ee8f675" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561207}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "787cf7fe-f2f7-5df0-b36f-e78b6273a4b5" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -2x - 3y =-4, l_{2}: 12x + 20y = 6$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &=-4 \\\\ 12x + 20y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 3y &=-4 \\\\\n-3y &= 2x - 4 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2x - 4}{-3} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x + 20y &= 6 \\\\\n12x + 20\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n12x - \\frac{40}{3}x + \\frac{80}{3} &= 6 \\\\\n-\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{80}{3} &= 6 \\\\\n-\\frac{4}{3}x &= - \\frac{62}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c788b1-e8d1-5ab2-b2ec-c639e5a5f429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561196} {:answer/id #uuid "78dd7c65-7c23-5532-976d-ff5e37ca8e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561224} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8afa02-2884-5634-93a8-7b7ccd61ae05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c788b1-e8d1-5ab2-b2ec-c639e5a5f429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561196} :answer-field/id #uuid "486aff25-f9b1-5424-a420-03217a3f6814" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561208}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7990b398-b163-5ff0-bd59-3b73f685ea5d" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -4x + y = 2, l_{2}: -12x + 3y =-15$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x + y &= 2 \\\\ -12x + 3y &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + y &= 2 \\\\\ny &= 4x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &=-15 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= -15 \\\\\n-12x + 12x + 6 &= -15 \\\\\n6 &= -15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805cb854-3cef-5a9d-b52f-6cb5f1a05d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561228} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd6325-a5dc-5571-807f-0a19cfc212a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561241} {:answer/id #uuid "f61301bd-60c9-56c5-bccb-3ea8e307b4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "805cb854-3cef-5a9d-b52f-6cb5f1a05d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561228} :answer-field/id #uuid "c843a425-7cc2-5a78-8427-4b2970f00770" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561249}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96e99e9b-5b2e-55b0-8814-cc28b8bf6bc8" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -x - y = 4, l_{2}: -12x - 3y =-12$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - y &= 4 \\\\ -12x - 3y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - y &= 4 \\\\\n-y &= x + 4 \\\\\ny &= -x - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-x - 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - 3y &=-12 \\\\\n-12x - 3\\left(-x - 4\\right) &= -12 \\\\\n-12x + 3x + 12 &= -12 \\\\\n-9x + 12 &= -12 \\\\\n-9x &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561204} {:answer/id #uuid "ce74c59e-9e7a-5fcf-9bfa-74ca29a5dc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561253} {:answer/id #uuid "eeaec689-8e5c-5fbe-a829-38566863fd86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561204} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90c2268-eb7e-5503-ad73-e1ac5a2b2e15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561254}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a01d9c5-2885-5132-9235-1d9478baed14" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = -x - 4, l_{2}: -9x - 3y = 15$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= -x - 4 \\\\ -9x - 3y &= 15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = -x - 4\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-x - 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-9x - 3y &= 15 \\\\\n-9x - 3\\left(-x - 4\\right) &= 15 \\\\\n-9x + 3x + 12 &= 15 \\\\\n-6x + 12 &= 15 \\\\\n-6x &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64762017-ef57-574d-99d7-a9be2892815d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561217} {:answer/id #uuid "8903af01-7bdb-59b7-bfc2-56796727445a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561231} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec78b20-d253-53dd-af36-f3b3e2a99e16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64762017-ef57-574d-99d7-a9be2892815d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c7459c3-7647-57df-ac62-0f53b2bd604d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561214}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4be2362-89eb-587e-82aa-d9d4f04eb125" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -5x - y = 5, l_{2}: -20x - 4y =-8$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x - y &= 5 \\\\ -20x - 4y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x - y &= 5 \\\\\n-y &= 5x + 5 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-20x - 4y &=-8 \\\\\n-20x - 4\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -8 \\\\\n-20x + 20x + 20 &= -8 \\\\\n20 &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "303e264e-f7bb-58e1-8f43-28746c565777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561201} {:answer/id #uuid "f84d8eb6-0a3f-5c54-b516-d5072df2722e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561263} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1ddb6a-6d38-5bf0-ac22-13dff12c39f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84d8eb6-0a3f-5c54-b516-d5072df2722e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561263} :answer-field/id #uuid "016fa648-d368-50d4-ab14-df62c0c4ad93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c74e2f77-c144-59ff-a39d-154078a44e94" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = 4x + 2, l_{2}: -8x + 2y = 6$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= 4x + 2 \\\\ -8x + 2y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = 4x + 2\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 2\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 8x + 4 &= 6 \\\\\n4 &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da3fcc3-fa0d-5f01-ba15-7551732faeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561210} {:answer/id #uuid "52d1d98a-2227-583b-995d-2d9f0f210a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561211} {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256} :answer-field/id #uuid "43673130-deba-5b98-8ce2-b4ee4ed0101a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561205}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7e53da6-3b28-54ab-be32-bc2afa7301df" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 5x + y =-1, l_{2}: -12x + 3y = 3$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x + y &=-1 \\\\ -12x + 3y &= 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &= 3 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(-5x - 1\\right) &= 3 \\\\\n-12x - 15x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf58711-5f7d-5d0c-9c8b-5e45dbfc55fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561200} {:answer/id #uuid "57e75c5c-9d7e-5fbb-9e68-fd683aeb2452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561212} {:answer/id #uuid "ea88b994-5abc-51ab-a610-96e8bfe4ffaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf58711-5f7d-5d0c-9c8b-5e45dbfc55fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561200} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3666b2-e413-595c-a093-783fa1dc8bf4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561245}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c878eb46-3c57-53bc-9b71-6029289efddf" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = x, l_{2}: -5x + 5y = 0$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ -5x + 5y &= 0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + 5y &= 0 \\\\\n-5x + 5\\left(x\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n-5x + 5x &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f19502-4a84-510e-96d9-21e50d95ed63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561202} {:answer/id #uuid "5d633272-a745-52f8-8022-869b2818e9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561215} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d8f10b-db63-5f68-bb23-678f2810b48b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d633272-a745-52f8-8022-869b2818e9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561215} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4562de-6958-5910-a9b5-816e85d031d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561194}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f855e10a-f1b4-5356-9c10-ccedf77e81d7" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -5x - 2y =-5, l_{2}: 20x + 8y = 21$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x - 2y &=-5 \\\\ 20x + 8y &= 21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x - 2y &=-5 \\\\\n-2y &= 5x - 5 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5x - 5}{-2} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x + 8y &= 21 \\\\\n20x + 8\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right) &= 21 \\\\\n20x - 20x + 20 &= 21 \\\\\n20 &= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e321ee9-c5ef-59e7-a720-449c297502e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561197} {:answer/id #uuid "96ad7a29-d44e-5997-8a2d-3dd126d93384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561235} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d98a33-6b71-5fc5-8f2b-3c8643f0ca6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e321ee9-c5ef-59e7-a720-449c297502e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561197} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fe7ee01-e7b5-51f5-a15c-7bbfebd4775e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561239}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe1a8df0-eeb5-5653-bde4-9ae932e3abc3" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 5x - 3y = 2, l_{2}: 20x - 12y = 7$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 3y &= 2 \\\\ 20x - 12y &= 7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 3y &= 2 \\\\\n-3y &= -5x + 2 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-5x + 2}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x - 12y &= 7 \\\\\n20x - 12\\left(\\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\\right) &= 7 \\\\\n20x - 20x + 8 &= 7 \\\\\n8 &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}]}
